        "id": 210703,
        "name": "Pydro",
        "username": "Pydro",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-12-18T20:16:06.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Arthur_Wynne\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/a3d4f5/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Arthur_Wynne:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>New poster here!Near Mint, but on the first try. I’ve never played with any of these variants before, and I have very little experience with AA in general, so there was no way I was getting through all of these power phases without a rewind or two to get all my ducks in a row. XPW Fanatic’s power is pretty good it turns out, especially against a villain with so much self-damage!I actually like Miss Information’s deck a lot better than it seems most people do - I don’t find it frustrating, but more of an interesting puzzle. But there’s no denying that when H=5, it’s pretty hard! At least for a Sentinels neophyte like me. So I’m feeling pretty good about my result. (Fanatic at 5 HP, everyone else KO when I finished her with a 23-point Wrathful Retribution - all of the others were wiped in the turn before, and if I had played correctly I probably could have kept everyone alive, but I saw that it would be very hard and that I would get her with Wrathful Retribution unless she got some kind of really silly draw, so I didn’t bother trying to go for a better result. Justice was served in the end, and that’s what counts, right? <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Welcome to the forums!</p>",
